\newlabel{tab:s2-label-entropy}{{C.9}{6}{Stratified PRM800K ranking by label entropy. On low-entropy traces, annotation labels are concentrated and all methods show compressed metrics, but \texttt {w\_struct} and Ridge still achieve NDCG@25\% above 0.99. On high-entropy traces, QP performs relatively closer to \texttt {w\_struct}, suggesting that explicit redundancy management becomes more useful when step-level discriminability matters}{table.9}{}}
